---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

const description =
  'From backlog to board: internal tickets, external sync, and spawning the SDLC chain for a ticket.';
---
<DocsLayout
  title="Ticketing"
  description={description}
  current="/docs/ticketing"
  prev={{ href: '/docs/healer', label: 'Healer' }}
  next={{ href: '/docs/visualizer', label: 'Visualizer' }}
>
  <p>
    Ticketing connects the factory to a queue of work: internal tickets you add with one command,
    or external tickets synced from another provider. Tickets flow through the
    <a href="/sssf/docs/visualizer">kanban board</a> (Backlog · Planning · Building · Reviewing ·
    Done/Blocked), and a backlog ticket can be run through the full SDLC chain with one command.
  </p>
  <p>
    Ticketing is optional and per-project: enable it in
    <code class="hl">adws/config/ticketing.yaml</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Commands</h2>
  <pre><code>sssf ticket add "Add a /health endpoint"     # create an internal backlog ticket
sssf ticket sync                              # fetch external tickets into the backlog
sssf ticket list                              # list tickets (id · provider · title · status)
sssf ticket run &lt;ticket_id&gt;                   # spawn simple_sdlc for a ticket</code></pre>
  <p>
    All four take <code class="hl">--project</code> to target a specific project;
    <span class="cmd">ticket run</span> also takes <code class="hl">--no-sandbox</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>How a ticket run works</h2>
  <pre><code>1. the ticket is marked starting, an adw_id is minted
2. the title + description are written to adws/prompts/&lt;slug&gt;.md
3. simple_sdlc is spawned with that prompt (sandboxed by default)
4. the ticket follows the run through the kanban stages
5. on completion the run's trace, branch sssf/&lt;adw_id&gt;, and the board agree</code></pre>
  <p>
    In sandboxed mode the prompt lives in the per-run worktree (no name-collision races) and is
    committed with the run. A ticket stuck in <code class="hl">starting</code> is returned to the
    backlog by the <a href="/sssf/docs/healer">healer</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Provider config</h2>
  <p>
    <code class="hl">ticketing.yaml</code> declares which providers are enabled. The
    <code class="hl">internal</code> provider needs no external credentials:
    <span class="cmd">sssf ticket add</span> works out of the box once enabled. External providers
    plug into <code class="hl">ticketing.sync_tickets()</code> and return sync results per provider
    (ticket counts or errors).
  </p>
  <div class="note" data-impeccable-ignore="side-tab">
    <strong>Ticket table.</strong> Tickets live in the project db
    (<code class="hl">tickets</code> table) with provider, external id, title, description, status,
    source url, and the run&rsquo;s adw_id when spawned.
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
